.policy "eslint-default-case-last" revision 4
.description "Put the default clause last in a switch statement; a default in the middle is easy to misread."
.language typescript
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// ESLint's default-case-last: a `default:` clause followed by another clause of the same switch.
//   switch (a) { default: f(); case 1: g(); }   → the default is reported
//   switch (a) { case 1: g(); default: f(); }   fine
// No options.
.violation default_case_last(at: node) code "default-case-last" "Default clause should be the last clause."
    suppress eslint "default-case-last"
    suppress oxlint "default-case-last"
    suppress biome "lint/suspicious/useDefaultSwitchClauseLast"
default_case_last(d) :- kind(d, "switch_default"), precedes(d, c), kind(c, "switch_case").
